1
00:00:00,075 --> 00:00:01,581
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:02,908
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:04,551 --> 00:00:05,881
(Episode 26)

4
00:00:05,923 --> 00:00:08,577
People can hear everything outside.
What's wrong with all of you?

5
00:00:09,069 --> 00:00:10,069
You...

6
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:13,487
Are you going to give me Seo Chon?
Have you thought about it?

7
00:00:15,377 --> 00:00:16,981
Seo Chon?

8
00:00:17,932 --> 00:00:19,388
Your house, give it to me,

9
00:00:19,902 --> 00:00:21,713
if you're really grateful to me.

10
00:00:25,882 --> 00:00:28,952
What have you ever lost?

11
00:00:29,527 --> 00:00:30,875
You have everything.

12
00:00:31,582 --> 00:00:35,474
The documents, two sons, a house.

13
00:00:36,917 --> 00:00:38,902
I only have one daughter...

14
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,534
and you didn't even let her go
to high school,

15
00:00:41,674 --> 00:00:43,748
and in the end,
you even took her bone marrow.

16
00:00:43,751 --> 00:00:45,560
Mom, please!

17
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:49,325
I can't forgive you.

18
00:00:50,542 --> 00:00:52,306
That's why I tried to die.

19
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,847
Because no one is on my side.

20
00:01:07,222 --> 00:01:08,985
You say I have everything?

21
00:01:09,317 --> 00:01:10,643
What do I have?

22
00:01:11,002 --> 00:01:13,495
My husband lives across the street
in another apartment...

23
00:01:13,498 --> 00:01:15,509
with my junior,
raising a daughter together.

24
00:01:16,298 --> 00:01:18,204
Do you think I could stay sane
living like that?

25
00:01:19,351 --> 00:01:21,170
That was your choice.

26
00:01:21,751 --> 00:01:24,406
- You could've set yourself free.
- I know.

27
00:01:24,988 --> 00:01:26,412
It was my choice.

28
00:01:27,742 --> 00:01:29,562
I chose to become a prison guard...

29
00:01:30,798 --> 00:01:32,613
just to keep you two locked in.

30
00:01:33,442 --> 00:01:34,869
You may feel trapped,

31
00:01:35,687 --> 00:01:37,993
but I'm just as trapped.

32
00:01:40,882 --> 00:01:42,590
Let's stop talking about this.

33
00:01:44,121 --> 00:01:45,121
I...

34
00:01:46,113 --> 00:01:49,094
think your daughter
is better than both of us.

35
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:53,410
Watching her has made me reflect a lot.

36
00:02:16,214 --> 00:02:17,599
Your mom wrote this.

37
00:02:26,662 --> 00:02:28,185
(I invested a lot in your dad's company.
You'll be okay financially.)

38
00:02:28,188 --> 00:02:29,817
(As I said, I don't resent you at all.
I'm just exhausted.)

39
00:02:44,629 --> 00:02:47,934
She's playing the victim,
when she's the one who caused harm.

40
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:53,440
Daughters really speak
without holding back.

41
00:02:55,222 --> 00:02:56,619
Seung Woo and I...

42
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,995
even when our mom frustrated us,
we could never say things like that.

43
00:03:00,742 --> 00:03:04,134
Why doesn't she just throw
all those documents away and start over?

44
00:03:06,142 --> 00:03:09,180
I used to think that in high school.

45
00:03:11,368 --> 00:03:14,746
Maybe she still loves my dad,
or is waiting for him.

46
00:03:15,997 --> 00:03:16,997
I used to think so.

47
00:03:18,806 --> 00:03:20,373
It's really hard.

48
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:22,883
Even so,
you shouldn't say things like that.

49
00:03:23,919 --> 00:03:27,113
Seeing her today,
your mom seems very fragile.

50
00:03:27,142 --> 00:03:29,454
She was always protected
and taken care of by my dad,

51
00:03:29,763 --> 00:03:31,385
so she never really had to grow up.

52
00:03:31,388 --> 00:03:33,756
Still, your mom wrote...

53
00:03:34,016 --> 00:03:35,731
that donating marrow to O Reum was kind.

54
00:03:36,041 --> 00:03:38,140
When I read that, I felt grateful.

55
00:03:38,757 --> 00:03:40,723
But she also asked for the Seo Chon house.

56
00:03:40,786 --> 00:03:43,071
Your mom just has a lot
of unresolved pain.

57
00:03:43,241 --> 00:03:44,937
Deep down, she's warm.

58
00:03:46,256 --> 00:03:48,102
You, as her daughter,
should try to understand her.

59
00:03:53,182 --> 00:03:54,325
When my mom...

60
00:03:55,165 --> 00:03:57,877
acts immaturely in front of other people,

61
00:03:59,527 --> 00:04:01,725
it's really embarrassing and upsetting.

62
00:04:02,182 --> 00:04:04,194
I told you, we feel the same way.

63
00:04:04,475 --> 00:04:05,708
But we hold it in.

64
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:08,104
If you say everything you want,
she'll just get hurt.

65
00:04:10,702 --> 00:04:11,702
And...

66
00:04:14,149 --> 00:04:15,984
I really hate to say this, but...

67
00:04:19,944 --> 00:04:23,221
your mom and dad had a good relationship.

68
00:04:24,322 --> 00:04:26,469
She probably fell into depression
after losing him so suddenly.

69
00:04:27,328 --> 00:04:28,560
My mom, on the other hand,

70
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:32,046
basically lived like a widow...

71
00:04:33,574 --> 00:04:34,976
so I guess it didn't affect
her the same way.

72
00:04:44,505 --> 00:04:47,748
We're not just women anymore.
We're mothers now.

73
00:04:47,801 --> 00:04:51,805
How can you think like that
with your child right in front of you?

74
00:04:51,876 --> 00:04:53,266
This isn't okay.

75
00:04:53,428 --> 00:04:55,240
Just give me the house.

76
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,429
Then let's live together.

77
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:00,990
I have nowhere else to go.

78
00:05:01,245 --> 00:05:04,113
If I give you that house,
you and I would have to live together.

79
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,511
Could you really do that?

80
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:07,384
We could just sell it and split the money.

81
00:05:09,616 --> 00:05:11,124
Say one more word...

82
00:05:11,127 --> 00:05:12,575
and I swear I'll cut you off for good.

83
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,809
You think I can't do it?

84
00:05:17,056 --> 00:05:19,179
There's a limit to how spoiled you can be.

85
00:05:19,536 --> 00:05:22,504
At your age,
venting like this is ridiculous.

86
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,840
I'm really disappointed in you.

87
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:28,799
If you take pills again next time,
I won't even blink.

88
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:30,304
I won't come either.

89
00:05:30,622 --> 00:05:33,965
Ji Ni, how can you say something so harsh?

90
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:35,940
Ma'am, please go.

91
00:05:36,816 --> 00:05:39,594
I think my mom is acting worse
because you keep accommodating her.

92
00:05:41,654 --> 00:05:42,767
Please go.

93
00:05:43,628 --> 00:05:45,174
You must be exhausted too,

94
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:46,940
taking care of O Reum
and dealing with our family.

95
00:05:47,133 --> 00:05:48,415
Go get some rest.

96
00:05:49,134 --> 00:05:50,134
I'll...

97
00:05:51,098 --> 00:05:52,455
stay here.

98
00:06:00,243 --> 00:06:01,637
If you pull that out,

99
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,000
I'm really cutting you off for good.

100
00:06:17,991 --> 00:06:20,012
(Captain's Library Publishing)

101
00:06:24,765 --> 00:06:26,355
Excuse me.

102
00:06:27,771 --> 00:06:29,094
Hello.

103
00:06:29,645 --> 00:06:33,186
- Yes, who are...
- Is Na Ji Ni here?

104
00:06:33,919 --> 00:06:36,617
She's out right now.
What do you need from her?

105
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,700
Please have this for lunch.

106
00:06:41,704 --> 00:06:44,959
Are you O Reum's mom?

107
00:06:45,039 --> 00:06:46,069
My goodness.

108
00:06:46,332 --> 00:06:50,060
- You know me? Yes, that's right.
- Hello.

109
00:06:50,487 --> 00:06:54,656
But if I accept this,
I think Ji Ni won't like it.

110
00:06:55,716 --> 00:06:59,298
Just tell her I dropped it off and ran,
and you couldn't stop me.

111
00:06:59,922 --> 00:07:00,992
Bye.

112
00:07:05,001 --> 00:07:06,134
What is this?

113
00:07:19,282 --> 00:07:21,665
You've really improved your taste
in movies.

114
00:07:22,041 --> 00:07:23,465
That's thanks to you, General.

115
00:07:24,348 --> 00:07:27,346
- Good. This is what I call culture.
- Yeah.

116
00:07:27,452 --> 00:07:28,530
Father.

117
00:07:30,268 --> 00:07:34,275
- What brings you here?
- Father, please help me.

118
00:07:34,681 --> 00:07:36,200
I'm really having a hard time.

119
00:07:37,052 --> 00:07:39,781
Have you eaten? Do you have time?

120
00:07:39,784 --> 00:07:42,344
I can take you somewhere nice.

121
00:07:42,382 --> 00:07:45,705
That sounds good, but how
about chicken porridge? It's summer.

122
00:07:45,708 --> 00:07:47,698
Chicken porridge?

123
00:07:48,656 --> 00:07:51,494
It's a free-range chicken raised
at a friend's farm.

124
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:54,840
How do you two...

125
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,536
Well, we've spent our whole lives
out at sea.

126
00:07:57,628 --> 00:07:58,819
I made it yesterday.

127
00:07:59,258 --> 00:08:00,913
- Have a seat.
- I'm fine.

128
00:08:00,942 --> 00:08:02,518
Feel free to talk.

129
00:08:02,536 --> 00:08:04,760
Sit down. It's nothing private.
You already know everything anyway.

130
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:06,111
Okay, just for a bit.

131
00:08:12,201 --> 00:08:13,548
It's really good.

132
00:08:13,641 --> 00:08:16,988
Right? It was a hit yesterday too.
Ji Hu ate a lot.

133
00:08:17,468 --> 00:08:19,115
He is driving me crazy.

134
00:08:19,313 --> 00:08:20,883
Don't say that.

135
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,750
Is he still upset about the painting?

136
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:24,059
Exactly.

137
00:08:24,322 --> 00:08:26,682
Don't you think
he's being way too sensitive?

138
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,932
Is that really something
to get this mad over?

139
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:31,882
Even if I'd spent hundreds of millions
on luxury goods, he'd be calmer.

140
00:08:31,965 --> 00:08:33,898
Buying luxury goods would've been better.

141
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:35,228
I just don't get it.

142
00:08:35,302 --> 00:08:37,536
Isn't a partner supposed to help
when things are hard?

143
00:08:37,607 --> 00:08:40,502
Let's eat first and talk.
I made dessert too.

144
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,280
- Is the tiramisu I made still there?
- Yes, it's ready.

145
00:08:53,207 --> 00:08:54,369
Did you call Ji Hu?

146
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,294
Yes, he'll be here soon.

147
00:08:59,077 --> 00:09:00,277
You called him?

148
00:09:00,361 --> 00:09:01,796
Isn't that what you came for?

149
00:09:02,249 --> 00:09:03,508
You two should make up.

150
00:09:03,511 --> 00:09:06,161
You're engaged. This shouldn't drag on.

151
00:09:06,458 --> 00:09:08,661
- He's really being cold.
- Do Hee.

152
00:09:10,319 --> 00:09:12,472
It's true that partners
should help each other,

153
00:09:12,475 --> 00:09:15,199
but it's just as important to understand
how the other person feels when you do.

154
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:16,942
That's the hard part for me.

155
00:09:17,062 --> 00:09:20,259
- He's so different from everyone else.
- That's what makes him Ji Hu.

156
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:22,473
If he were like everyone else,
he'd just be anyone.

157
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,531
From now on, why don't you ask first
before making any decisions?

158
00:09:26,534 --> 00:09:28,652
Then I'll ask you, Father.

159
00:09:28,654 --> 00:09:30,673
Good. Let's do that.

160
00:09:43,359 --> 00:09:44,411
Ji Hu?

161
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,552
You should practice peeling fruit.

162
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,361
I'm too nervous to watch.

163
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,395
The housekeeper will do it anyway.

164
00:09:51,439 --> 00:09:53,002
Once we're married, we'll have to do it.

165
00:09:53,073 --> 00:09:54,375
Will we have a housekeeper as newlyweds?

166
00:09:54,382 --> 00:09:56,534
My mom will get one for us. Don't worry.

167
00:09:58,706 --> 00:10:00,698
- Did I do it wrong again?
- Yeah.

168
00:10:01,607 --> 00:10:02,777
Are you upset?

169
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:04,519
No.

170
00:10:04,942 --> 00:10:08,832
I was worried about how we'd get along.

171
00:10:10,407 --> 00:10:11,885
Thank you, Ji Hu.

172
00:10:11,948 --> 00:10:13,275
You're all I have, Ji Hu.

173
00:10:13,355 --> 00:10:15,025
Hey, I'm holding a knife.

174
00:10:15,485 --> 00:10:17,409
That's why the housekeeper should do it.

175
00:10:18,795 --> 00:10:20,588
It's been so long since I heard you laugh.

176
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:23,919
Mother.

177
00:10:25,628 --> 00:10:29,423
I'm letting it slide
because Ji Hu begged me.

178
00:10:29,426 --> 00:10:31,287
I really was going to end things with you.

179
00:10:31,325 --> 00:10:33,035
No, Mother.

180
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:35,646
How could you swing your handbag at me?

181
00:10:35,873 --> 00:10:36,996
Does that make sense?

182
00:10:37,462 --> 00:10:40,521
- Even now, just thinking about it...
- Please don't think about it.

183
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:43,540
Forget it ever happened, okay?

184
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:46,565
Just be more careful.

185
00:10:47,894 --> 00:10:49,496
Okay.

186
00:10:50,833 --> 00:10:53,475
Mother, how about a sauna tomorrow?

187
00:10:53,902 --> 00:10:55,661
I'll take you for the full package,

188
00:10:55,755 --> 00:10:57,952
and help you get rid of all that stress.

189
00:10:59,422 --> 00:11:02,327
- Fine. Let's do that, then.
- Yes.

190
00:11:16,819 --> 00:11:17,859
Ji Hu.

191
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:20,416
Ji Hu.

192
00:11:24,159 --> 00:11:25,330
Sorry.

193
00:11:26,597 --> 00:11:29,482
Even if you were up all night,
how could you do this?

194
00:11:29,542 --> 00:11:31,644
I was trying to reach someone
at the Vienna Philharmonic,

195
00:11:31,869 --> 00:11:33,700
so I was up nearly all night.

196
00:11:34,492 --> 00:11:37,061
Sorry. Did you watch it alone? Was it fun?

197
00:11:37,064 --> 00:11:38,713
It wasn't fun at all.

198
00:11:39,283 --> 00:11:40,283
I'm leaving.

199
00:11:41,351 --> 00:11:42,424
I'll take you home.

200
00:11:46,466 --> 00:11:48,400
Ji Hu, wait.

201
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:58,957
What? Do you have something to say?

202
00:12:07,272 --> 00:12:10,752
We never talked much
about your bullying in middle school.

203
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,786
I told you that was a false accusation.

204
00:12:15,802 --> 00:12:16,961
Anyway...

205
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:19,617
I didn't discuss it further
because it was in the past.

206
00:12:20,024 --> 00:12:22,027
Right. It's in the past.

207
00:12:22,222 --> 00:12:23,532
It's all over now.

208
00:12:25,132 --> 00:12:26,171
And...

209
00:12:26,314 --> 00:12:29,021
because I know how easily
your mother sways you...

210
00:12:29,023 --> 00:12:30,454
I held back for that reason too.

211
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,358
I didn't want to ruin
everything we've shared.

212
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,498
- I feel the same.
- But this is happening now.

213
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,850
Things like this will keep happening.

214
00:12:39,186 --> 00:12:42,250
Not everything I do will work out,
so please promise me this.

215
00:12:45,562 --> 00:12:48,505
Whatever it is, talk to me first.

216
00:12:48,677 --> 00:12:51,755
- Don't decide on your own.
- Okay.

217
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,860
Don't scare me like that either.

218
00:12:55,270 --> 00:12:56,270
Okay.

219
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:57,836
Let's go.

220
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,434
We're closed.

221
00:13:11,035 --> 00:13:12,660
You're tough.

222
00:13:13,359 --> 00:13:15,290
If you were a man,
I would've fallen for you.

223
00:13:18,475 --> 00:13:21,338
- Who won?
- I won by a landslide.

224
00:13:22,336 --> 00:13:24,841
It's two out of three,
but your mother keeps losing.

225
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:27,305
How could a mother who tried to die
and leave her child behind win?

226
00:13:27,308 --> 00:13:29,519
- She can't argue back.
- How did you get out?

227
00:13:29,602 --> 00:13:31,988
She pushed my buttons again
and I went after her.

228
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:34,041
She pretended to sleep, so I left.

229
00:13:34,189 --> 00:13:36,077
She should give up already.

230
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:37,721
She can't win this time.

231
00:13:38,010 --> 00:13:40,933
Even if I consider her depression
after losing her husband,

232
00:13:40,935 --> 00:13:42,725
I still can't understand her.

233
00:13:43,157 --> 00:13:45,182
Everything she says is complete nonsense.

234
00:13:45,881 --> 00:13:50,102
"Go on blind dates. Get married.
Love is everything. Quit your job..."

235
00:13:51,393 --> 00:13:53,174
"Take the Seo Chon house and sell it."

236
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:58,288
I'm impressed you haven't blown your lid.

237
00:14:02,722 --> 00:14:04,761
I really respect my dad.

238
00:14:05,552 --> 00:14:08,444
How did he spend his whole life
trying to please my mom?

239
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:11,550
- I guess that really was love.
- Hey.

240
00:14:11,586 --> 00:14:12,938
Don't even mention the L in love.

241
00:14:12,997 --> 00:14:14,790
Lions, lemons, lollipops.

242
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:17,909
- Is she being discharged tomorrow?
- Yeah.

243
00:14:18,306 --> 00:14:21,017
I have no idea how I'll live with her.

244
00:14:21,081 --> 00:14:23,620
- Maybe I'll just stay at my studio.
- You can't.

245
00:14:23,961 --> 00:14:25,746
Her stomach must still be weak.

246
00:14:25,805 --> 00:14:27,923
You should make her porridge
and nourishing meals.

247
00:14:27,925 --> 00:14:29,367
That's what daughters do.

248
00:14:31,325 --> 00:14:34,487
I should finish cleaning.

249
00:14:36,930 --> 00:14:38,281
Seriously...

250
00:14:48,448 --> 00:14:49,825
You big fool.

251
00:14:50,212 --> 00:14:51,317
You're so stubborn.

252
00:14:52,535 --> 00:14:54,435
Fine, you're right. Just eat for now.

253
00:15:02,842 --> 00:15:03,868
Once Ji Ni gets here,

254
00:15:04,282 --> 00:15:05,854
I'll arrange my discharge,

255
00:15:06,661 --> 00:15:08,442
so stop pretending to care and leave.

256
00:15:09,015 --> 00:15:10,188
Let's not see each other again.

257
00:15:11,202 --> 00:15:13,252
Seung Hyun already handled your discharge.

258
00:15:13,555 --> 00:15:14,886
Come stay at our place.

259
00:15:16,068 --> 00:15:17,859
Your stomach wall is badly damaged.

260
00:15:18,128 --> 00:15:20,342
It'll be hard for Ji Ni to care for you.

261
00:15:20,422 --> 00:15:22,400
She has to go to work too, right?

262
00:15:22,975 --> 00:15:23,979
Stay for two days...

263
00:15:24,254 --> 00:15:27,008
No, just stay for one day
and let me prepare some light meals.

264
00:15:27,075 --> 00:15:30,598
I'm not familiar with your kitchen,
so I can't cook for you there.

265
00:15:30,762 --> 00:15:31,768
What's gotten into you?

266
00:15:31,795 --> 00:15:33,288
I don't have a husband
for you to take from me.

267
00:15:33,368 --> 00:15:34,394
Se Ri,

268
00:15:34,949 --> 00:15:37,001
we're too old to be talking like this.

269
00:15:37,669 --> 00:15:38,695
Mom.

270
00:15:39,308 --> 00:15:40,814
You came early.

271
00:15:41,702 --> 00:15:43,839
- The hospital bill...
- We took care of it.

272
00:15:44,753 --> 00:15:45,753
What?

273
00:15:46,565 --> 00:15:49,100
Good. It's the least you should do.

274
00:15:54,088 --> 00:15:55,104
Ji Ni,

275
00:15:55,372 --> 00:15:56,900
I already mentioned it to your mom,

276
00:15:57,023 --> 00:15:59,309
but could she stay at our home
for a day or two?

277
00:15:59,788 --> 00:16:01,311
You have to go to work,

278
00:16:02,501 --> 00:16:05,690
and she needs to eat rice porridge
several times throughout the day.

279
00:16:06,339 --> 00:16:07,784
You mean in Seo Chon?

280
00:16:15,535 --> 00:16:16,800
It's so heavy.

281
00:16:19,388 --> 00:16:22,336
What on earth did you bring?
I need to get to work...

282
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:24,188
I know.

283
00:16:24,255 --> 00:16:25,675
I'll give you these and leave.

284
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,287
Thank you.

285
00:16:30,641 --> 00:16:31,846
I'm exhausted.

286
00:16:33,608 --> 00:16:36,707
Put the meat and frozen fish
in the freezer,

287
00:16:36,824 --> 00:16:38,504
and these are cosmetics,

288
00:16:38,506 --> 00:16:41,188
a bag that will look good on you,
and some clothes.

289
00:16:42,888 --> 00:16:44,126
You can trust my taste.

290
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:45,668
I bought half the department store.

291
00:16:47,055 --> 00:16:50,375
- You really didn't have to...
- I know.

292
00:16:50,708 --> 00:16:53,430
You tried to save O Reum
without telling anyone.

293
00:16:53,735 --> 00:16:55,535
That made it even more touching.

294
00:16:56,561 --> 00:16:58,800
It's really nothing. Just...

295
00:16:59,501 --> 00:17:01,995
accept them as O Reum's way
of thanking you.

296
00:17:03,775 --> 00:17:06,419
Remember when I used
my father-in-law's card last time?

297
00:17:06,475 --> 00:17:08,702
I'm that kind of woman.
Spending money is my specialty.

298
00:17:10,515 --> 00:17:13,001
In that case, I'll accept one bag.

299
00:17:13,003 --> 00:17:14,626
I'd feel guilty refusing them all.

300
00:17:14,628 --> 00:17:15,990
Take them, or I'll leave them and run.

301
00:17:16,415 --> 00:17:18,401
Please, don't do this.

302
00:17:21,302 --> 00:17:22,961
You've seen how O Reum is doing.

303
00:17:23,955 --> 00:17:27,475
O Reum is getting better every day,
and I want to give you whatever I can.

304
00:17:28,248 --> 00:17:30,284
This is the least I could do.

305
00:17:33,695 --> 00:17:35,573
Thank you so much.

306
00:17:38,375 --> 00:17:39,609
Father.

307
00:17:40,239 --> 00:17:41,792
Thank you.

308
00:17:45,702 --> 00:17:47,315
Don't worry about your mother.

309
00:17:47,761 --> 00:17:50,598
I bought lots of groceries
and even got abalone.

310
00:17:50,628 --> 00:17:52,012
I'll make sure she eats properly,

311
00:17:52,015 --> 00:17:54,047
and bring her home when she's better.

312
00:17:54,049 --> 00:17:55,842
Don't worry about anything.

313
00:17:59,475 --> 00:18:01,450
I feel like I'm in the middle of a storm.

314
00:18:02,161 --> 00:18:03,892
It's all so overwhelming.

315
00:18:08,482 --> 00:18:12,105
This is a nice house, though.

316
00:18:14,012 --> 00:18:15,015
Why?

317
00:18:15,849 --> 00:18:17,136
You want it?

318
00:18:19,382 --> 00:18:22,707
I'm no different from your mom
asking for the Seo Chon house.

319
00:18:22,892 --> 00:18:24,117
We're even.

320
00:18:26,065 --> 00:18:27,227
That's true.

321
00:18:36,102 --> 00:18:38,405
- Is that you, Mom?
- Yeah.

322
00:18:41,822 --> 00:18:43,669
What? Did you see a ghost?

323
00:18:44,479 --> 00:18:45,521
You're here.

324
00:18:51,635 --> 00:18:53,421
Bone marrow sure works wonders.

325
00:18:53,542 --> 00:18:55,277
The tables have really turned.

326
00:18:56,568 --> 00:18:59,190
I heard you were so cruel to your dad.

327
00:18:59,204 --> 00:19:01,352
You wouldn't even let him
set foot in this yard.

328
00:19:03,281 --> 00:19:05,282
Put the bags upstairs.

329
00:19:05,725 --> 00:19:08,307
- Se Ri, go inside.
- Okay.

330
00:19:15,308 --> 00:19:17,167
Mai took care of everything
before she left.

331
00:19:17,548 --> 00:19:18,568
Sit here.

332
00:19:23,775 --> 00:19:26,225
What can I get you?
Want some more rice porridge?

333
00:19:28,428 --> 00:19:30,008
Nothing's changed, right?

334
00:19:31,082 --> 00:19:33,161
You're such a stubborn fool.

335
00:19:33,588 --> 00:19:35,202
That's just how I am.

336
00:19:35,568 --> 00:19:38,086
What's the point of switching rooms?
I live alone.

337
00:19:40,502 --> 00:19:42,384
Lie down. You must be tired.

338
00:19:43,287 --> 00:19:45,038
I'm going to sleep.
Go take care of your things.

339
00:19:45,095 --> 00:19:46,990
Okay. I will.

340
00:20:11,635 --> 00:20:13,007
Did she have a baby?

341
00:20:13,668 --> 00:20:14,915
It's good for helping
her recover her strength.

342
00:20:14,968 --> 00:20:17,090
How could you give up the master bedroom?

343
00:20:17,288 --> 00:20:19,684
I really don't understand you, Yeong Ju.

344
00:20:20,436 --> 00:20:21,850
Did you forget already?

345
00:20:21,935 --> 00:20:23,771
They saved O Reum's life.

346
00:20:23,773 --> 00:20:25,888
What wouldn't I do? They saved my child.

347
00:20:26,588 --> 00:20:28,840
I'd even dance in my underwear
if they asked me to.

348
00:20:30,328 --> 00:20:32,591
I can't tell if it's your vitality...

349
00:20:32,779 --> 00:20:34,159
or just stubbornness.

350
00:20:34,868 --> 00:20:37,709
- Stop talking and peel the garlic.
- Okay.

351
00:20:39,441 --> 00:20:40,444
O Reum,

352
00:20:40,552 --> 00:20:42,196
this is the world you changed.

353
00:20:42,464 --> 00:20:44,882
It's a whole new world.

354
00:20:49,218 --> 00:20:51,218
(Captain's Library Publishing)

355
00:20:56,101 --> 00:20:57,407
You go ahead.

356
00:20:58,105 --> 00:21:00,594
- I need to catch up on some work.
- Okay.

357
00:21:01,643 --> 00:21:03,105
Are you sure that's okay?

358
00:21:04,102 --> 00:21:05,938
Shouldn't you be taking care of your mom?

359
00:21:06,562 --> 00:21:08,067
She's not at home.

360
00:21:08,279 --> 00:21:09,285
She...

361
00:21:10,655 --> 00:21:12,661
Things have been difficult between us,

362
00:21:13,549 --> 00:21:15,173
so she went somewhere
more comfortable for her.

363
00:21:15,175 --> 00:21:16,394
It's better for me too.

364
00:21:16,695 --> 00:21:18,223
Then I'll leave it to you.

365
00:21:18,495 --> 00:21:19,773
I'll head out first.

366
00:21:20,414 --> 00:21:21,428
Okay.

367
00:21:31,585 --> 00:21:34,628
Sir, could you take a look
at the piano in the hall?

368
00:21:34,866 --> 00:21:35,866
Sure.

369
00:21:36,648 --> 00:21:38,701
I know you're busy,
so I wouldn't call otherwise.

370
00:21:39,128 --> 00:21:40,780
We really need your expertise.

371
00:21:41,782 --> 00:21:43,234
Rehearsal is tomorrow afternoon.

372
00:21:48,528 --> 00:21:50,234
You're on board, right?

373
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:52,592
Yes. Understood.

374
00:21:52,702 --> 00:21:55,094
You know the hotel
has been changed, right?

375
00:22:06,462 --> 00:22:07,871
My sweet daughter.

376
00:22:09,902 --> 00:22:11,946
I don't blame you.

377
00:22:13,201 --> 00:22:14,561
You did the right thing.

378
00:22:16,782 --> 00:22:18,496
You suffered so much...

379
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:20,542
because you had me as your mother.

380
00:22:23,055 --> 00:22:24,188
Mom,

381
00:22:24,317 --> 00:22:28,048
why can't I call you Mom when we're out?

382
00:22:35,108 --> 00:22:36,524
I'm sorry, Ji Ni.

383
00:22:38,672 --> 00:22:40,040
I'm so sorry.

384
00:22:55,048 --> 00:22:57,482
Your body must've been through
quite a shock.

385
00:22:57,548 --> 00:22:59,165
You need to loosen up.

386
00:23:00,022 --> 00:23:03,321
You've got so much energy,
and you're pretty ambitious too.

387
00:23:03,889 --> 00:23:06,128
I know. I'm pretty ambitious.

388
00:23:08,468 --> 00:23:10,402
Please forget about...

389
00:23:11,057 --> 00:23:12,600
that house I went to see.

390
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,601
Please forgive me.

391
00:23:15,868 --> 00:23:17,225
Depends on how you behave.

392
00:23:25,235 --> 00:23:27,880
She brought some abalone,
so I only added a little.

393
00:23:27,882 --> 00:23:29,308
I wasn't sure how your stomach
was feeling.

394
00:23:29,415 --> 00:23:30,981
Try some with the white fish.

395
00:23:31,035 --> 00:23:33,340
Save the abalone for later
when you get home.

396
00:23:35,259 --> 00:23:38,212
I went to the fish market with Seung Hyun.

397
00:23:38,641 --> 00:23:42,063
I put some meat and other things
in your fridge at home too.

398
00:23:42,142 --> 00:23:44,419
I also got Ji Ni a few things,
like cosmetics.

399
00:23:44,909 --> 00:23:47,361
It's not much, but it's from the heart.

400
00:23:48,095 --> 00:23:49,334
Please accept them.

401
00:23:52,435 --> 00:23:55,075
You two should go.
You have dinner to make too.

402
00:24:04,108 --> 00:24:05,871
I'll eat this and head home.

403
00:24:06,214 --> 00:24:09,196
Why? Stay the night.

404
00:24:09,391 --> 00:24:11,648
I just stopped by. I was upset.

405
00:24:11,875 --> 00:24:13,790
I'm doing much better now.

406
00:24:15,115 --> 00:24:18,021
Promise me you won't take
those pills again. Okay?

407
00:24:18,548 --> 00:24:20,348
Didn't you want me dead?

408
00:24:20,913 --> 00:24:22,325
Not anymore.

409
00:24:37,821 --> 00:24:38,821
Yes?

410
00:24:40,508 --> 00:24:41,575
Mom?

411
00:24:43,682 --> 00:24:44,825
Okay.

412
00:24:48,355 --> 00:24:49,667
She's so fickle.

413
00:24:58,248 --> 00:25:00,300
- I called a cab.
- Okay.

414
00:25:03,348 --> 00:25:05,875
If you run into trouble at work,
give me a call.

415
00:25:05,922 --> 00:25:07,694
I know plenty of people
in the production business,

416
00:25:07,769 --> 00:25:09,986
- so I'll help if I can.
- Forget it.

417
00:25:10,388 --> 00:25:12,252
It's better if we stay out
of each other's lives.

418
00:25:14,108 --> 00:25:15,108
Yeong Ju,

419
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:18,025
thanks for everything.

420
00:25:20,375 --> 00:25:22,848
- Did O Reum's parents go to the hospital?
- Yeah.

421
00:25:24,655 --> 00:25:26,225
I hope O Reum makes a full recovery.

422
00:25:26,852 --> 00:25:28,019
As for us,

423
00:25:28,182 --> 00:25:29,661
let's just go our separate ways.

424
00:25:30,272 --> 00:25:31,995
That's for the best, right?
I'm right, aren't I?

425
00:25:35,801 --> 00:25:37,140
Take care, Yeong Ju.

426
00:25:53,501 --> 00:25:54,805
Ji Ni.

427
00:25:55,364 --> 00:25:56,588
Ji Ni.

428
00:26:12,341 --> 00:26:13,341
Honey,

429
00:26:14,444 --> 00:26:17,188
I think it's really over now.

430
00:26:19,448 --> 00:26:22,215
We won't have to worry
about a kidney transplant, right?

431
00:26:29,782 --> 00:26:32,823
It was uncomfortable there,
so I came here.

432
00:26:42,241 --> 00:26:44,138
Are you really not going to talk to me?

433
00:26:44,567 --> 00:26:46,515
- No.
- What?

434
00:26:46,588 --> 00:26:48,681
I don't want to talk to you for a while,

435
00:26:48,709 --> 00:26:50,695
- so don't talk to me.
- Na Ji Ni.

436
00:26:50,697 --> 00:26:53,063
Do I have to keep calling you Mom...

437
00:26:53,157 --> 00:26:54,819
when you were willing
to leave me behind and die?

438
00:26:55,328 --> 00:26:57,588
When I tried to kill myself, you told me,

439
00:26:57,708 --> 00:26:59,477
"You can't do that to your parents."

440
00:26:59,844 --> 00:27:00,848
What about you?

441
00:27:01,088 --> 00:27:02,859
Can you do that to your child?

442
00:27:03,488 --> 00:27:06,596
I'm so angry I can't stand it.

443
00:27:06,870 --> 00:27:07,881
I...

444
00:27:12,742 --> 00:27:13,852
And another thing.

445
00:27:14,180 --> 00:27:16,019
Don't trash my room again.

446
00:27:16,582 --> 00:27:18,888
You can do whatever you want
with your life,

447
00:27:19,051 --> 00:27:20,163
but not my room.

448
00:27:20,222 --> 00:27:23,140
- I made that room for you.
- Then should I move out?

449
00:27:23,306 --> 00:27:24,310
Want me to leave?

450
00:27:24,531 --> 00:27:25,541
You little brat.

451
00:27:25,808 --> 00:27:28,708
How can someone so heartless
make animation?

452
00:27:28,710 --> 00:27:29,935
You need a good heart.

453
00:27:29,975 --> 00:27:31,915
All the animations I watch
have devoted daughters.

454
00:27:31,917 --> 00:27:33,867
I don't draw devoted daughters,
so don't worry.

455
00:27:35,515 --> 00:27:36,533
And...

456
00:27:36,754 --> 00:27:38,681
I don't like your playing either, Mom.

457
00:28:05,401 --> 00:28:08,687
(Family Register)

458
00:28:08,761 --> 00:28:10,906
- Would you be okay if I became an orphan?
- It's because of you.

459
00:28:10,908 --> 00:28:13,370
You betrayed me
and laughed with the Seo Chon family.

460
00:28:13,373 --> 00:28:14,400
You're jealous, right?

461
00:28:14,403 --> 00:28:16,242
Just because I don't love someone,
does that mean no one else can?

462
00:28:16,244 --> 00:28:17,782
It's a shame he's gone.

463
00:28:17,784 --> 00:28:19,833
He left behind such a beautiful wife
and sons.

464
00:28:19,835 --> 00:28:21,230
I tried to kill myself once.

465
00:28:21,232 --> 00:28:22,353
Why are you so shocked?

466
00:28:22,355 --> 00:28:24,022
I've always wanted to die.

467
00:28:24,024 --> 00:28:25,479
Let's go back to Nam San.

468
00:28:25,481 --> 00:28:27,851
This time, let's smile instead of crying.

469
00:28:28,940 --> 00:28:30,940
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
